 "description": "BIGVILLE R11 (block 259000) -- SCOPE-GATING, the compute thesis (HEADLINE). An IN-SCOPE agent carries the activity wiring (active_beat/active_clock) and is MATCHED by bw_run_in_scope (it RUNS each tick: last_beat<-clock.epoch, age+1); an OUT-OF-SCOPE agent is a bare PERSISTED node with NO wiring, so the matcher never scans it -> ~0 compute (DORMANT), its attrs byte-identical across dormant ticks. bw_dissolve_on_leave is the DEPARTURE->dormant DECISION (ties R8): a wired agent with left==1 (R8 dream collapse) has its activity wiring DISSOLVED (del_edge) and goes in_scope=0/dormant=1 -- it walks off the edge of scope and dissolves into the frontier, state persisted. FALSIFIER: ablate scope-gating (wire the whole world) -> every agent is matched and RUNS -> per-tick cost grows with the TOTAL world (measured ~linear), the cost we must NOT pay. Composes existing Terms (Lt/Eq/Plus, del_edge/set_attr effects); zero new Rust.",
